# What never enters a build context.
#
# One file, two images: Dockerfile.web and Dockerfile.backend both build from
# the repository root, so every rule here applies to both. Two effects, and the
# second is the one that matters:
#
#   speed   the context is tarred and sent to the daemon before the first
#           instruction runs. node_modules and .next are hundreds of megabytes
#           of files that are rebuilt inside the image anyway.
#   safety  a file that is not in the context cannot be COPYed in by accident,
#           not by a future `COPY . .`, not by a careless edit. An image layer
#           is readable by anyone who can pull the image, and deleting a secret
#           in a later layer does not remove it from the earlier one.

# ---- secrets. See "Safety" in my-app/CLAUDE.md. --------------------------
#
# .env carries DJANGO_SECRET_KEY and GEOSERVER_PASSWORD. It is read by
# `docker compose` on the HOST at run time and must never be inside an image.
# .env.example is the template and is deliberately still allowed in, since it
# holds no real value.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
secrets/

# ---- version control and agent state -------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# ---- node ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# node_modules is reinstalled by `npm ci` from the lockfile inside the image.
# Copying the host's copy in would also bring the host's platform-specific
# native binaries (SWC, Tailwind oxide, lightningcss), which is how a build on a
# Mac produces an image that cannot start on Linux.
**/node_modules
my-app/.next
my-app/out
my-app/build
my-app/coverage
my-app/test-results
my-app/playwright-report
my-app/blob-report
my-app/*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*

# ---- python --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# .pyc files are compiled for one interpreter version. The image's Python is
# 3.12 and this repository's machine runs 3.14, so copying them in ships
# bytecode that is silently ignored at best.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# ---- local state that is not the application -----------------------------
#
# A developer's SQLite database and workspace must not be baked in: the image
# would ship someone's half-finished runs, and the named volumes that replace
# them would never be used because the path already had content.
services/backend/db.sqlite3
services/backend/db.sqlite3-*
**/rangeland-workspace

# ---- editor and OS noise -------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea
.vscode

# ---- documentation -------------------------------------------------------
#
# Left OUT of the ignore list on purpose: services/backend/README.md and
# contracts/*.md are small, and contracts/ must reach the backend image whole
# because settings.py reads criteria.json and ahp-fixtures.json from it.
